  "body": "As [reported against the W3C](https://github.com/w3c/html/issues/1590), HTML's specification is unclear about what paragraphs are. In particular, section 4.4.1 \"The p element\" defers to 3.2.5.4 to define what a paragraph is. But 3.2.5.4 defines 2 types of paragraphs:\r\n\r\n1. A lengthy definition not based on the `<p>` element (\"Let view be a view of the DOM that replaces all...\").\r\n2. \"A paragraph is also formed explicitly by p elements.\", which defers to section 4.4.1.\r\n\r\nSo 4.4.1 defers to 3.2.5.4, which partially defers to 4.4.1. Effectively, this states that some things are paragraphs, but fails to define what is not a paragraph.\r\n\r\nNote that section 3.2.5.4 \"Paragraphs\" has several self-links (3 in the first note, 1 in \"A paragraph is also formed explicitly by p elements.\").",
